  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Rack spaces can hold small wet projects; a tag records the owner and the earliest safe handling time.\", \"decision\": \"How should projects use the drying rack?\", \"goal\": \"Help members make steady progress while sharing tools, work surfaces, materials, and responsibility for the studio.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood craft studio serves members working on small personal projects. It has bookable benches, ordinary hand tools, shared consumables, a drying rack, labeled storage, a message board, and a steward during opening hours. Members follow the same basic safety rules. Helpers can support brief activities without taking over the whole room, and each decision concerns a separate routine.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe steward assigns drying-rack spaces after reading members’ handling-time tags and places shorter drying jobs near the front. Projects likely to leave soon remain accessible without disturbing those that need longer.\nMembers reserve drying-rack spaces for expected finishing times and attach handling-time tags when their projects arrive. Visible reservations help members pace wet work around the rack capacity available later in the session.\nMembers choose an empty drying-rack space and attach the handling-time tag when placing a wet project there. The person preparing the project records when it can move, giving later users a clear basis for planning."
    }
  ],
